    {
      "term": "connection time",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 转机衔接时间；前一程航班抵达与后一程航班出发之间可用于转机的时间。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "转机时间",
        "转机衔接时间"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "connection times"
      ],
      "en": "Our connection time was short, so we went straight to the next gate.",
      "zh": "我们的转机衔接时间很短，所以直接去了下一个登机口。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.britishairways.com/content/en/sg/information/airport-information/flight-connections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "check-in deadline",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 值机截止时间；必须完成办理值机手续的最后时刻，区别于登机时间。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "值机截止时间",
        "办理值机截止时间"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "check-in deadlines"
      ],
      "en": "I finished checking in just before the check-in deadline.",
      "zh": "我赶在值机截止时间之前办完了值机手续。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.britishairways.com/content/en/de/information/legal/conditions-of-carriage/general-conditions-of-carriage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "miss a connection",
      "partOfSpeech": "verb phrase",
      "meaning": "① 没赶上衔接的下一程交通班次；航空语境中指错过转机航班。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "错过转机",
        "没赶上转机",
        "错过衔接航班"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "missed a connection",
        "missing a connection",
        "misses a connection"
      ],
      "en": "We could miss a connection if the first flight arrives late.",
      "zh": "如果第一程航班晚到，我们就可能赶不上衔接的下一程航班。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.britishairways.com/content/en/sg/information/airport-information/flight-connections",
        "https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/miss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "stop button",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 下车提示按钮；公交车上按下后向司机示意要在下一站下车的按钮。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "下车按钮",
        "公交下车按钮",
        "下车提示按钮"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "stop buttons"
      ],
      "en": "I pressed the stop button as the bus approached the library.",
      "zh": "公交车接近图书馆时，我按下了下车按钮。",
      "references": [
        "https://bus.osakametro.co.jp/en/guide/usage/cat/how_to_ride_the_bus.php",
        "https://busready.bctransit.com/courses/busready-online-course/lessons/lesson-7/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "bus service suspension",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 公交服务暂停运行；某条线路或某段公交服务暂时停止提供，不只是一个站点暂不停靠。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "公交车停运",
        "公交停运",
        "公交服务暂停"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "bus service suspensions"
      ],
      "en": "The bus service suspension meant we had to walk to the station.",
      "zh": "公交服务暂停运行，我们只好步行去车站。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.stagecoachbus.com/promos-and-offers/east-midlands/skegness-services"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "move-in checklist",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 入住检查清单；入住时逐项核对房屋、设备等现有状况的清单。这里不是搬家物品打包清单。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "入住检查清单",
        "入住验房清单"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "move-in checklists"
      ],
      "en": "We noted the cracked window on the move-in checklist.",
      "zh": "我们在入住检查清单上记下了窗户的裂纹。",
      "references": [
        "https://studentlegal.uiowa.edu/know-the-law/tenants-rights/moving"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "hand over the keys",
      "partOfSpeech": "verb phrase",
      "meaning": "① 交接钥匙；把钥匙交给接收的一方，常用于房屋交接，不是另配一把钥匙。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "交接钥匙",
        "移交钥匙"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "handed over the keys",
        "handing over the keys",
        "hands over the keys"
      ],
      "en": "The landlord will hand over the keys when we meet at the flat.",
      "zh": "我们在公寓见面时，房东会把钥匙交给我们。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.braintree.gov.uk/news/article/909/new-community-centre-completed-in-witham"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "lease expiry",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 租约到期；租约原来约定的期限届满。到期本身不说明是否续租或必须如何搬离。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "租约到期",
        "租赁合同到期"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "lease expiries"
      ],
      "en": "She put the lease expiry date in her calendar.",
      "zh": "她把租约到期日记在了日历上。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.bury.gov.uk/business/business-property/council-owned-land-and-property"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "renew a lease",
      "partOfSpeech": "verb phrase",
      "meaning": "① 续租；续签租约，使原有租赁关系延续到新的期限。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "续签租约",
        "续租",
        "续签租赁合同"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "renewed a lease",
        "renewing a lease",
        "renews a lease"
      ],
      "en": "The tenants asked whether they could renew their lease for another year.",
      "zh": "房客们询问能否再续租一年。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.fife.gov.uk/council-and-democracy/land-and-property/community-groups-and-sports-clubs/apply-to-lease"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "deduction from the deposit",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 押金扣款；从已交付的押金中扣除的一部分钱。词语本身不表示这项扣款一定合理或合法。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "押金扣款",
        "从押金中扣款"
      ],
      "englishForms": [
        "deductions from the deposit"
      ],
      "en": "The statement listed a deduction from the deposit for a missing key.",
      "zh": "结算单列出了一笔因钥匙遗失而从押金中扣除的钱。",
      "references": [
        "https://www.gov.uk/guidance/technical-guidance-for-official-receivers/29-solely-owned-tenanted-property"
      ]
    },
    {
      "term": "maintenance request",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun phrase",
      "meaning": "① 维修申请；向负责方提出、请其检查或修理设备或房屋问题的请求。",
      "chineseAliases": [
        "维修申请",
        "维修请求",
        "房屋维修申请"
